1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:05,483
Meet NurseBridge, a browser-call intake demo using
fictional patient information.

2
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:14,869
A demo administrator creates a private workspace, then
invites a caller into a separate browser session.

3
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:27,322
The caller joins the queue and starts intake. In this
walkthrough, the words come from a labeled mock
transcript replay, not microphone transcription.

4
00:00:30,800 --> 00:00:38,881
The nurse sees arrival order, the caller's draft, and
links to the original reported words. Queue position
is not a clinical urgency ranking.

5
00:00:43,800 --> 00:00:52,983
Corrections stay visible as revisions. Here, yesterday
becomes this morning. An unmeasured temperature
remains unmeasured, and every fact still needs nurse
review.

6
00:00:56,800 --> 00:01:06,123
The nurse can take over the browser call. After both
sides connect, two-way human audio replaces automated
forwarding. The caller speaks directly with the nurse.

7
00:01:09,800 --> 00:01:19,501
NurseBridge collects context for human review. It does
not diagnose, triage, or determine that waiting is
safe. This demonstration uses only synthetic data.
